The correct response is:


Which of the following is true about the following code?

void *b = (void *)malloc(sizeof(int));
int *a = (int *)b;
printf("a is %p and b is %p\n", a, b);

The answer is "a is 8 and b is 8".

A programmer writes a program that contains a bug that may be found when executing a particular test case. The program is recompiled with a new compiler. Will the bug still appear? Explain.
